            0.113,
            0.274,
            0.812,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Check your answers by thinking about the movement in the mineshaft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.313,
            0.72,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Adding, subtracting, and comparing any numbers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.342,
            0.836,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To add and subtract even larger integers, we can imagine even larger lifts! In fact, we can imagine a lift that can extend forever upwards and forever downwards, starting from Level 0. There does not even have to be any building or mine around — just an ‘infinite lift’!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.44,
            0.833,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can use this imagination to add and subtract any integers we like."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.471,
            0.834,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For example, suppose we want to carry out the subtraction + 2000 – (–200). We can imagine a lift with 2000 levels above the ground and 200 below the ground. Recall that,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.547,
            0.768,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Target Level – Starting Level = Movement needed"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.577,
            0.834,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To go from the Starting Floor –200 to the Target Floor + 2000, we must press + 2200 (+ 200 to get to zero, and then + 2000 more after that to get to + 2200). Therefore, (+ 2000) – (– 200) = + 2200."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.645,
            0.587,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that (+ 2000) + (+ 200) is also + 2200."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.68,
            0.833,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try evaluating the following expressions by similarly drawing or imagining a suitable lift:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.73,
            0.633,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": [
